{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652619-suggestion-elder-s-behavior","id":652619,"title":"Suggestion elder's behavior","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-05T08:44:08-07:00","id":652619,"title":"Suggestion elder's behavior","content":"This is the situation: <br /> During a blood party in an house of an elder vampire, a PC decide to feed (and it's ok becouse was in line with the general mood of the party) from a young slave, and to make her a ghoul unseen. Then he ask to the owner of the slave to buy her, without said her taht he made the slave a ghoul. <br /> The elder accept and organizes the exchange for the next night. <br /> Well...for sure tue elder find out that the slave become a ghoul, and she could get angry to be not adviced befor right? So I thought about some kind of punishment:<br /> the eleder could kill the slave and sell the dead body, faking naturalness, directly during the exchange saing: &quot;oh I didn't say you last night but I decided to feed from her till death&quot; or something similar (sorry for bad english <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> But probably an elder vampire could think about something more underhand, maybe to keep the PC under control without let him to know about it. Can you give me some advice? Do you have more intersting ideas?<br /> thanks a lot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T09:13:06-07:00","id":652668,"title":"","content":"The elder can probably inflict a full blood bond on the ghoul, which would break the PCs blood bond and let them have a ghoul that's devoted to the elder for at least a year.<br /> <br /> If the elder's a ventrue or has dominate, some sort of Entombed Command might be reasonable, or shifting the ghoul's memories around so that they think the PC hurt them horribly somehow so that the thought of vengeance is always in them.<br /> <br /> If the elder was childish, they could just blood bond every other mortal in the PCs life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T11:38:42-07:00","id":652851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652619-suggestion-elder-s-behavior?p=652668#post652668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the elder's a ventrue or has dominate, some sort of Entombed Command might be reasonable, or shifting the ghoul's memories around so that they think the PC hurt them horribly somehow so that the thought of vengeance is always in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh! Chain of Command the ghoul to wait until the PC takes her back to his haven, then Command him to kill her! Then the elder still gets paid for a slave he obviously didn't care that much to keep, since he was willing to sell her in the first place, the PC loses the ghoul, and it's done by the PC's hand within his own Haven, so the elder has plausible deniability.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's none of my business what he does with her, she's his property now. Though, why he would buy a slave simply to murder her is beyond me. Ah, but no matter. Any stake I may have had in her life ended when I accepted his payment.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T12:44:06-07:00","id":652936,"title":"","content":"I like all of your suggestion. I need just a mechanic's explanation about the use of dominate in this way:<br /> If the elder uses entombed command with iron edict on the PC saing: &quot;When you are in front of the guards, kill &quot;the ghoul's name&quot;. Now...after speking that command, the PC remembers or understands to be dominated??? I means, he could be tring to avoid the specific trigger right?<br /> <br /> If yes, could the elder use, after that fist domination, the lying mind to delete this memory and, for pure sadism, use another time entombed command to let the memory of the domination come back only after the kill? Just to let the PC knows that she wanted to punish him???<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T12:49:50-07:00","id":652941,"title":"","content":"No, no, Chain of Command. Page 142. It's a Devotion that lets you use Dominate to give someone a Command to then go give another person a Command (temporarily allowing them use of Dominate at your level). So, you would Chain of Command the ghoul &quot;when you get to (PC's name)'s house, use Dominate to tell (PC's name) 'Stab me to death.'&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T13:04:50-07:00","id":652946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652619-suggestion-elder-s-behavior?p=652941#post652941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, no, Chain of Command. Page 142. It's a Devotion that lets you use Dominate to give someone a Command to then go give another person a Command (temporarily allowing them use of Dominate at your level). So, you would Chain of Command the ghoul &amp;quot;when you get to (PC's name)'s house, use Dominate to tell (PC's name) 'Stab me to death.'&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I know. I refered to the general dominate mechanics? Without that devotions. Just to know for future application <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T13:34:01-07:00","id":652967,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest that the elder would just have a much lower opinion of the PCs. They commited a breach of ettiquette, and they failed to cover it up. They haven't actually done anything to the elder, they've gained whatever they got from the trade, the PCs didn't really get anything from the deal. The elder could well just see them as a bunch of idiots (maybe spread that story around Elysium a bit so every one thinks they're idiots too).<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the elder could see them as useful pawns. They failed to cover for their mistake, but it wasn't a bad attempt. Plus, the elder now has leverage over them. A good elder could do a lot with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T13:44:15-07:00","id":652978,"title":"","content":"nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7657-gloom","user":"Gloom","date":". 09-05-2015, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7657-gloom","name":"Gloom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T14:00:49-07:00","id":653017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652619-suggestion-elder-s-behavior?p=652946#post652946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes I know. I refered to the general dominate mechanics? Without that devotions. Just to know for future application <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, gotcha. Sorry, I misunderstood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652619-suggestion-elder-s-behavior?p=652936#post652936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the elder uses entombed command with iron edict on the PC saing: &quot;When you are in front of the guards, kill &quot;the ghoul's name&quot;. Now...after speking that command, the PC remembers or understands to be dominated??? I means, he could be tring to avoid the specific trigger right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. The victim has to have the Mezmerized Condition for the vampire to use Entombed Command on them, and part of the Mezmerized Condition is that when it ends, you don't remember what happened while you were Mezmerized. So, basically the Elder first uses Mezmerize to put the PC into a trance. Then while they're in that trance state, the elder uses Entombed Command to implant a trigger, such as &quot;when you are in front of the guards.&quot; What happens when the PC encounters that trigger depends on what level of Dominate you use along with Entombed Command. In your example, it sounds like you want to use Iron Edict to implant the command &quot;Kill [ghoul's name].<br /> <br /> When the initial trance ends, the PC has no memory of being given the command, but when they encounter the trigger (being in front of the guards), they will gain the Dominated Condition and must carry out the command (kill [ghoul's name].) Part of the Dominated Condition is that once it ends, you don't remember what happened while you were Dominated, so the PC would just black out when he saw the guards, and when he came to, the ghoul would be dead, her blood all over him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652619-suggestion-elder-s-behavior?p=652936#post652936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If yes, could the elder use, after that fist domination, the lying mind to delete this memory and, for pure sadism, use another time entombed command to let the memory of the domination come back only after the kill? Just to let the PC knows that she wanted to punish him???</div> </div> </div> </div>You could probably use The Lying Mind to restore the memory of what happens while the victim was Mezmerized and/or Dominated, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T16:56:31-07:00","id":653161,"title":"","content":"Thank you all. You have been very helpful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T18:04:17-07:00","id":653273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652619-suggestion-elder-s-behavior?p=652851#post652851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh! Chain of Command the ghoul to wait until the PC takes her back to his haven, then Command him to kill her! Then the elder still gets paid for a slave he obviously didn't care that much to keep, since he was willing to sell her in the first place, the PC loses the ghoul, and it's done by the PC's hand within his own Haven, so the elder has plausible deniability.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's none of my business what he does with her, she's his property now. Though, why he would buy a slave simply to murder her is beyond me. Ah, but no matter. Any stake I may have had in her life ended when I accepted his payment.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> That's terribly wicked. Sometimes I don't know if should admire you or be afraid.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":