l=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's terribly wicked. Sometimes I don't know if should admire you or be afraid.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Is it bad that I find this incredibly flattering?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-05-2015, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T03:46:07-07:00","id":653681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652619-suggestion-elder-s-behavior?p=653456#post653456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Is it bad that I find this incredibly flattering?</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably adds to the &quot;be afraid&quot; camp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T04:36:51-07:00","id":653711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gloom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652619-suggestion-elder-s-behavior?p=652978#post652978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nevermind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shame that. I thought your point about player buy-in was well made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T12:37:26-07:00","id":654249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652619-suggestion-elder-s-behavior?p=653444#post653444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think with Auspex 2 for examples.<br /> Anyway can't she simply &quot;smell&quot; kindred vitae in a mortal as well as the Kindreds smell other vampires? I read a vampire always know if he is in front of another kindred, smelling or touching him etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>A ghoul is not a vampire, I don't think there's any way to really tell a ghoul and a mortal apart unless they do a ghoul thing right in front of you.<br /> <br /> That said, auspex 2 would probably reveal something weird was up and with some further investigation and questioning of the slave would probably do. Does the elder habitually use auspex on their slaves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T13:54:43-07:00","id":654366,"title":"","content":"Ghouls store vitae in similar fashion to vampires, normal mortals don't. Ghouls also register as Blood Potency 0. So they're going to register as something not entirely human. Vampires are also hyper attuned to the presence of blood without requiring Auspex, so I don't think it's at all unreasonable to say a typical vampire can smell vitae on the breath of a human who recently imbibed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T19:32:05-07:00","id":654668,"title":"","content":"(I'm not an expert on 2nd ed, so I may be missing slight differences between 1st and 2nd)<br /> How would you detect vitae stored in a ghoul? I don't think 2nd ed is entirely clear on how and where it is stored. If it's in the stomach being able to smell it seems a bit cheesy. And I'm also not sure a BP of 0 would/should show up to kindred - predatory aura refers to the beast and vampires specifically. I couldn't find a wording either way in the book. Smelling vitae on the breath, however, certainly rings true. I forget about kindred senses fairly regularly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T20:27:01-07:00","id":654723,"title":"","content":"Does Vitae have a smell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T22:02:47-07:00","id":654744,"title":"","content":"VtR 2e, pg 98:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blood bearing Vitae is slightly darker, and has an almost<br /> syrupy quality. It has all the normal metallic smells blood<br /> should, but also has a subtle, sweet smell, like a dessert wine. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T22:40:24-07:00","id":654773,"title":"","content":"Ah, yes. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T22:52:03-07:00","id":654775,"title":"","content":"My players were curious about detecting ghouls, too. After scouring the book I came to the conclusion that the best you could do is try and smell blood or vitae on the ghoul and make an educated guess. But there's reasons other than being a ghoul to have vitae on them, like Vinculum.<br /> <br /> I'd probably have it be impossible to smell after a night (but it'd stay that whole time; vampires can smell and see the smallest traces, so washing won't help). I'd base this on how long it takes for vitae to lose its potency for feeding, since there's nothing more specific I can find.<br /> <br /> I didn't find anything explicit in the book one way or another, though regarding ghoul detection.<br /> <br /> Still, back the the original question, if he smells the Vitae, there's really nothing the vitae could be that wouldn't make the elder upset, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T06:05:06-07:00","id":655051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenagain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/652619-suggestion-elder-s-behavior?p=654668#post654668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'm not an expert on 2nd ed, so I may be missing slight differences between 1st and 2nd)<br /> How would you detect vitae stored in a ghoul? I don't think 2nd ed is entirely clear on how and where it is stored. If it's in the stomach being able to smell it seems a bit cheesy. And I'm also not sure a BP of 0 would/should show up to kindred - predatory aura refers to the beast and vampires specifically. I couldn't find a wording either way in the book. Smelling vitae on the breath, however, certainly rings true. I forget about kindred senses fairly regularly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of the opinion that ghoul detection falls into the same category as vampire detection when one vampire encounters another. Their Beast reacts to the predatory aura of the vampire that was imprinted (via willpower expenditure) on the ghoul when he was made and there's lots of ways to describe it, you just change the nuances to differentiate. For instance, you can describe to a player that their vampire character gets the taste of blood in the back of their throat and their gums above their fangs itch for a moment whenever they encounter a vampire. If it's a ghoul, their fangs itch but they don't get the taste of blood.<br /> Maybe they just notice the ghoul doesn't quite move the same way as normal humans because they have had their speed, stamina, or strength permanently enhanced (via the first physical discipline they got when they were made a ghoul) but not with the same predatory vibe as another vampire.<br /> Maybe they hear a faint sloshing sound and catch a brief smell of blood to signal the presence of vitae. And that simply what tells them the individual is a vampire or ghoul then at that point it simply becomes a matter of checking for a heartbeat or breathing to know if the person is alive or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-07-2015, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T07:46:48-07:00","id":655108,"title":"","content":"A vampire can taste it via a Taste of Blood. Personally, I prefer ghouls to be easily hidden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T08:22:22-07:00","id":655178,"title":"","content":"Me too. I guess that's what it comes down to, really. I prefer vampires to be unable to just detect ghouls. They don't have a beast and it makes them more of a hidden threat to other vampires..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}